  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Value Chain development in the Kurdish Region of Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the relatively stable but fragile context of the Kurdish Region of Iraq, agriculture contributes 8% to the GDP and employs about 70% of the population. Most agriculture is traditional and small-scale, though the sector has great potential and opportunity for modernizing.Within the scope of this project, a capacity building project is formulated that is based on local needs and that contributes to strengthening of an agriculture value chain. The selection of a specific crop, that is produced in the Sulaymaniyah region, will be part of the first phase of the project. Besides capacity building, establishing linkages and better cooperation between the different actors in the selected value chain will be part of the next step.  Development and strengthening of a specific value chain should not only create new jobs but also increase the income of value chain actors, increase export potential and improve local market supply with better quality and more sustainably produced vegetables and reduced food loss.</narrative>
  </description>
